-- title:
--   Finite-type fine moduli package for Γ₀(N)×Γ(ℓ) level data
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a Noetherian commutative ring (in a fixed universe), let $\ell$ be a prime with $3\le\ell$ and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, and assume the images of $\ell$, $N$, $2$ and $3$ in $A$ are units. Two equivariance hypotheses are imposed, each for all $A$-algebras $T$ in that universe: first, for every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every tuple $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ in $T$, if $D$ is a level-$\ell$ structure on $W$ — both points satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishes at $x_P$ and at $x_Q$, and the two elements $\mathrm{indepElt}\,W\,\ell\,x_P\,x_Q=\prod_{1\le a\le(\ell-1)/2}\bigl(x_Q\Psi^2_a(x_P)-\Phi_a(x_P)\bigr)$ and its companion with $x_P,x_Q$ interchanged are units — then the transformed tuple $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ is a level-$\ell$ structure on $C\bullet W$; second, for all $p,k$ and every $h\in T[X]$ with `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (that is, `W.IsTwoKernel h` if $p^k=2$, and `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise), the polynomial $u^{-2d}\,h(u^2X+r)$, where $d=1$ if $p^k=2$ and $d=\varphi(p^k)/2$ otherwise, has the same property for $C\bullet W$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a package $P$ finely representing the moduli datum obtained from the product level component $\mathtt{gamma0PowComponent}\,A\,N\times(\mathtt{levelPComponent}\,A\,\ell\times\mathtt{LevelComponent.trivial})$: an $A$-algebra $P.B_0$ with a universal point such that every point of the datum over any $A$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal one under a unique $A$-algebra map $P.B_0\to T$. Here points over $T$ are classes, modulo variable change, of Weierstrass curves over $T$ with invertible discriminant together with a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $N$ satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` at exponent $v_p(N)$, a level-$\ell$ structure, and a point of the one-element trivial component. Moreover $P.B_0$ is of finite type over $A$ and integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by the element $P.j_0$ (the $j$-invariant of the universal point).
--
--   This is the representability step for the rigidified moduli problem of Weierstrass curves with $\Gamma_0(N)$-type cyclic prime-power kernel data and a Katz $\Gamma(\ell)$-basis, with the third (Drinfeld) slot taken trivial, in the style of the fine moduli theory of Katz–Mazur; the finiteness assertions are what make the resulting affine ring usable. It is invoked in the later identification of the moduli ring with power-series charts and in the comparison of maximal ideals with $q$-expansions.
